# Weekly audit of the 3D printing library's CATALOGUE.md against the disk
# (`print` plugin, /Volumes/local/3DPrinter/Models). `--fix-counts` heals the
# one class a script can settle on its own -- a Formats number that no longer
# matches the files -- and the Notes column is never touched.
#
# A nonzero exit is the notification, and it means a finding a person has to
# settle: a row whose folder is gone, or a model folder with no row. An
# unmounted /Volumes/local exits nonzero too, which is the same signal for a
# different reason, and the log says which.
#
# /usr/bin/python3 on purpose: the script is stdlib-only, and the system
# interpreter is the one that is there whatever else a launchd environment
# lacks. `sd` resolves through JOB_PATH, which cron-jobs.sh builds with
# ~/bin/common and ~/.local/bin.
#
# The lock check rides along because nothing else runs it: edit sd-plugin.json
# and sd-plugin.lock goes stale in silence. Both commands run whatever the
# other does -- `&&` would let a catalogue finding hide a drifted pin -- and
# the job exits nonzero if either did.
JOB_SCHEDULE="0 9 * * 0"          # Sundays, 09:00
JOB_COMMAND='rc=0; /usr/bin/python3 /Volumes/local/3DPrinter/Models/_scripts/audit_catalogue.py --fix-counts || rc=$?; sd plugin lock --check /Volumes/local/3DPrinter/Models || rc=$?; exit $rc'
JOB_DIR="/Volumes/local/3DPrinter/Models"
JOB_PROMPT=""
JOB_MODEL=""
JOB_CLAUDE_ARGS=""
